---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	description:
		"Aerobic point values for walking and running distances of one to fifteen miles, from Running Around Portland (1979).",
	title: "Aerobic Point Tables",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta} wide>
	<h1 class="title mb-2">Aerobic Point Tables</h1>
	<p class="text-muted mb-8 text-sm">Appendix from <em>Running Around Portland</em> (1979).</p>
	<div class="prose lg:prose-lg prose-cactus">
		<p>
			The following tables give aerobic point values for walking and running distances from one
			to ten miles at 1/2 mile increments, with the exception of the 12.5 mile distance. From ten
			to fifteen miles the increments are given at the mile mark, with the exception of the 12.5
			mile distance. For more detailed increments to 1/10 mile, see the appendix to "The New
			Aerobics," by Dr. Ken Cooper. Data used in the tables were obtained directly from the
			Institute for Aerobics Research and are somewhat revised from the tables in the book. Point
			scores are in the third column.
		</p>
	</div>
	<figure class="not-prose mt-6">
		<img
			src="/appendix/aerobic-point-tables.jpg"
			alt="Aerobic point tables for running and walking distances from 1 to 15 miles, giving a point score by finishing time"
			class="w-full rounded-sm border border-muted/30 bg-white"
		/>
		<figcaption class="text-muted mt-2 text-sm">Scanned from the original book.</figcaption>
	</figure>
	<p class="mt-12">
		<a class="cactus-link" href="/appendix/">← Back to appendices</a>
	</p>
</PageLayout>
